      <h1>a</h1>
      <p>The shortest identifier a row may carry</p>
      <p>The shortest identifier a row may carry, with a paragraph behind it, so that a page whose file is found by the shortest name there is proves the join works at that end of the range.</p>
      <p>What it needs before it is any use is a second paragraph, because a file carrying exactly one is a file that cannot show whether the order paragraphs arrive in survives the read.</p>
      <p>What it does with data about a person is nothing, and saying so is the point: this paragraph exists so that a page carrying no data line and a page carrying one are two different pages in this fixture.</p>
      <p>The plugin is being built. Nothing finished is published for it, so there is nothing to install and installing what is in the repository would add nothing a user can see.</p>
      <p>The plugin is built in the repository Fixture/jellyfin-plugin-a, and what this page says about it is read from the roster rather than written here.</p>
